From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Viewer-relative camera, controls and listener

In AR the viewer's head is the camera, so the game's own camera output is
replaced where it matters. All of it requires gArMode.

- the camera node uses an identity view and no screen roll, and object
  frustum culling is skipped: the whole diorama is in view. Lakitu still
  runs; only its view output is discarded.
- adds the game hook table (src/game/ar_game_hooks.h, gArGameHooks, NULL by
  default). The stick, pole and star-dance facing use its control_yaw, so
  the stick is relative to the viewer; billboards and cylboards face the
  head; every positional sound's source vector is taken in the head's
  listener space.
- the object draw distance is infinite, the far plane is raised and the
  depth cull is skipped, without touching the user's saved configDrawDistance.
- the cannon Mario aims from stays drawn and its barrel follows the aim
  (gArCannonVisible, default on; off is vanilla).
